Z||000000||Pretender||03-19-2000||06:49 PM||||after i remove the dogbone and the two bolts holding the cradle up? i don't want to drop it too far down.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||fiero56||03-19-2000||10:15 PM||||If you just unhook the dogbone and pull the two verticle cradle bolts, it would only be "safe" to hinge it only an inch or two. The fuel lines(at least on the v-6) don't leave much room for slack. Depending on how far you want to drop it, I disconnect the fuel lines, shift + select cables, slave cylinder from it's mounting bracket, a/c compressor, and a few coolant lines on the firewall side.  <BR>If you only need a few inches, disconnect the fuel lines, and shift/select cables, along with the dogbone. And lower very slowly, watching for any snags.||||reg||1
